WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.340
<v Instructor>So let's take a look at the inner workings</v>

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.120
of the EC2 Instance Connect service and feature

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.800
that uses the SendSSHPublicKey API.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.890
So we have an EC2 instance and its own security group.

5
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.150
And on the inbound rules,

6
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.470
we're going to allow SSH on port 22 from a particular source

7
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.580
and that source contains the prefixes, the IP ranges

8
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.220
that works for the EC2 Instance Connect service.

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.410
So that's how you get it from this URL.

10
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.690
But the idea is that we open up port 22

11
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:34.470
so that we can actually SSH into the instance.

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.760
Now, a user will access the EC2 Instance Connect API

13
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.660
and then what is going to happen

14
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.083
is that whenever we initiate an EC2 Instance Connect,

15
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.550
behind the scene, it's going to upload push

16
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.810
as a one-time thing

17
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.710
and SSH public key onto the EC2 instance.

18
00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.810
That key is valid for 60 seconds

19
00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.900
and that is the SendSSHPublicKey API.

20
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.350
So this API allows the EC2 Instance Connect service,

21
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.290
but really you could use it as well yourself,

22
00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:09.000
to upload a specified SSH key on the EC2 instance.

23
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.010
That means that for 60 seconds,

24
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.870
you have the opportunity to connect

25
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.250
using the private corresponding key into your EC2 instance.

26
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.670
And this is how the EC2 Instance Connect service works.

27
00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.270
It's by uploading very shortly an SSH public key

28
00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.830
that allows you privately

29
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.500
to connect to it within 60 seconds.

30
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.210
So just something you need to know.

31
00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.400
And any connection then,

32
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.840
because it's going to be using this SendSSHPublicKey API

33
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.720
and also if you use the EC2 Instance Connect API,

34
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.280
it will be logged in CloudTrail

35
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.830
so you have full audit and visibility.

36
00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.420
Okay, that's it, I hope you liked it

37
00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.370
and I will see you in the next lecture.

